      "costUsd": 0.0071475,
      "pronunciationText": "This video starts something new: random variables. Here's a die from a board game, rolled two hundred times. A four came up thirty-eight times. Let's watch all two hundred rolls land, and fill in the other faces. Four came up more than any other face. So is the die fair? Before we can answer, we need to know what the counts from a fair die should look like. That's what a probability distribution tells us. So how do data, and a model, each give us a distribution?"
    },
