      "inputTokens": 120,
      "outputTokens": 775,
      "costUsd": 0.0070350000000000005,
      "pronunciationText": "First, a name for the number we're recording. A random variable is a number decided by the outcome of a chance experiment. Here, X is the number on the top face. It's discrete, which means its values are separate, and we can list them: one, two, three, four, five and six. We write P of X equals four for the probability that X takes the value four. Capital X is the variable, and small x stands for any one of its values. When it's clear which variable we mean, we just write P of x."
    },
