      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 111,
      "outputTokens": 808,
      "costUsd": 0.0073275,
      "pronunciationText": "Add the six unrounded estimates and you get exactly one. But adding them only shows that it happens. Here's why it has to happen. Every roll lands on exactly one face. No roll is counted twice, and none is missed. So the six counts add to two hundred, the total number of rolls. Divide that total by two hundred, and you get one. That works for a complete, one-value-per-trial count, so unrounded estimates from data always add to one. Rounded ones can be a little off."
