      "outputTokens": 791,
      "costUsd": 0.007176500000000001,
      "pronunciationText": "What we've built is a probability distribution. It's the set of values X can take, together with the probability of each value. We show it two ways. A table gives the exact numbers we calculate with. A bar graph shows the shape. The bars stand apart, because X takes no values in between. Every probability must be between zero and one, and together they must add to one. Both checks matter. These three numbers add to one, but minus zero point four can't be a probability, so this list isn't a distribution."
