      "inputTokens": 153,
      "outputTokens": 1173,
      "costUsd": 0.0106335,
      "pronunciationText": "Often there's no data, just ay description, and we generate the distribution ourselves. Toss a fair coin three times, and let X be the number of heads. Each sequence of tosses gives exactly one value of X. Step one, list the values. X can be zero, one, two or three. Step two, find each probability. There are eight equally likely sequences, and three of them have exactly one head, so P of one is three eighths. Step three, check. One eighth, three eighths, three eighths and one eighth are each between zero and one, and they add to one. The graph shows something the table hides. It's symmetric, and the middle values are three times as likely as the ends."
    },
