      "pronunciationText": "X can be zero, one or two. Call the counters red one, red two, yellow one and yellow two. There are six possible pairs, all equally likely. One pair has no reds, four pairs have one red, and one pair has two reds. So the probabilities are one sixth, four sixths and one sixth, and they add to one. One third each is wrong. Three values don't have to be equally likely."
